    "summary": "Mellow early‑70 set with stellar Mason’s Children and King Bee",
    "blurb": "The Honolulu show delivers a concise, relaxed first set that builds to an energetic Pigpen finale. Highlights include Mason's Children, a slower Me & My Uncle, and a cleanly captured King Bee. Recording quality is excellent for a 1970 SBD, making it one of the best early‑70 tapes.",
    "review": "On January 24, 1970 the Grateful Dead took the stage at Honolulu Civic Auditorium for a brief but memorable single‑set performance. Jerry Garcia’s guitar shines on Mason's Children and Black Peter, while his phrasing on Me & My Uncle is deliberately slower yet still compelling. Pigpen (Ron McKernan) closes the set with a rousing \"I'm A King Bee\" that feels like a natural climax to the mellow flow. The soundboard capture by Kaplan is remarkably clean for its era—reviewers call it “awesome” and note it’s the cleanest Mason's Children they’ve heard, despite occasional drop‑outs and a tiny pitch correction. The set ends with a tasteful Feedback segue into \"And We Bid You Good Night,\" followed by an encore of Good Lovin'. For anyone interested in early‑70 Dead material, this recording offers both high‑fidelity sound and strong performances.",
